  "instagram_caption": "Would you rather have put $1,000 into Warren Buffett's company in 1964, or into the whole stock market?\n\nFrom 1964 to the end of 2025, the S&P 500 with dividends gained 46,061% overall, about 10.5% a year. $1,000 became $461,610. Berkshire Hathaway's per-share market value gained 6,099,294%, about 19.7% a year. $1,000 became about $61 million. That's 132 times more, from a gap of about 9 points a year.\n\nWhat did you guess before the counter stopped?\n\nSource: Berkshire Hathaway 2025 shareholder letter (performance table). Past results don't guarantee future returns. Not financial advice.\nFollow @the_real.number for the real number behind your money.\n\n#warrenbuffett #compounding #investing #stockmarket #therealnumber",
